{
  "requirement": "Maps node and criterion paths to a record under the configured root. `load` returns `None` for a missing record. `store` atomically replaces the record.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct FileEvidenceStorage { /* private fields */ }\n\nimpl FileEvidenceStorage {\n    pub fn new(root: impl Into<PathBuf>) -> Self;\n    pub fn record_path(&self, path: &NodePath, criterion: &CriterionPath) -> PathBuf;\n    pub async fn load<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> Result<Option<Record<N, L>>, FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: DeserializeOwned + Send,\n        L: DeserializeOwned + Send;\n    pub async fn store<N, L>(\n        &self,\n        path: &NodePath,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<N, L>,\n    ) -> Result<(), FileStorageError>\n    where\n        N: Serialize + Sync,\n        L: Serialize + Sync;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for FileEvidenceStorage;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests adequately cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.filesystem-storage.FileEvidenceStorage`.\n\n**Path mapping (`record_path`, keying under the configured root)**\n- `tests/storage.rs#fn[paths_are_injective_and_loading_missing_records_has_no_side_effects]` asserts exact `record_path` results under the root. It covers empty paths, empty segments, multiple segments, `/`, `..`, NUL, control characters, non-ASCII text, and a combining-character form.\n- `tests/storage.rs#fn[source_and_criterion_boundaries_preserve_independent_records]` asserts the exact paths for node and criterion splits that could collide. After storing, it reloads every record and checks each one is independent.\n\n**`load` returns `None` for a missing record**\n- The first test calls `load` on a root that does not exist. It asserts `is_none()` for every path, then asserts `!root.exists()`, so a missing load has no side effects.\n- The boundaries test also asserts `None` before each `store`.\n- `load` errors are covered in `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]`. It checks malformed JSON and type-incompatible data give `Json`, and a directory in place of the record gives `Io`. It also checks the stored record round-trips.\n\n**`store` atomically replaces the record**\n- `tests/storage.rs#fn[failed_serialization_preserves_records_and_failed_replacement_cleans_up]` has two checks. A serialization failure leaves the original bytes unchanged. A failed replacement returns `Io` and leaves only `record.json` in the directory, with no stray temporary file.\n- `fn[concurrent_readers_only_observe_complete_records_from_competing_writes]` runs two writers replacing a large record 30 times each while a reader loads concurrently. Every observed record is complete and internally consistent, and only the expected single directory entry remains at the end.\n- The boundaries test asserts the record's directory holds only `record.json` after each store.\n\n**Signatures and the `Clone` implementation**\n- `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` compares rustdoc's inherent member signatures and trait implementations against the requirement's declaration block, in `check_declaration`. So `new`, `record_path`, `load`, `store`, and `impl Clone` are checked against the declaration.\n- `Clone` is used at compile time by `#[derive(Clone)]` on `StoredGraph` in `tests/support/stored_graph.rs`, which holds a `FileEvidenceStorage`. The `store.clone()` in the concurrent test clones an `Arc`, so it does not exercise `Clone` itself.\n- `Clone` carries no conditional or transformation of its own, so this is sufficient.\n\nI found no unacknowledged gap.",
